{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1194751-alternative-setting-idea-vampires-disappear-and-are-replaced-by-revenants","id":1194751,"title":"Alternative setting idea: Vampires disappear and are replaced by Revenants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-12T23:56:08-07:00","id":1194751,"title":"Alternative setting idea: Vampires disappear and are replaced by Revenants","content":"So a while ago I had an idea pop into my head, which is that for some unknown reason (perhaps Antediluvian related) the vampires were all eliminated sometime in the Middle Ages. What is left of Caine's Bloodline are the Revenants families, who have survived into the modern nights and have created their own organizations and politics. <br /> <br /> I worked on the setting a bit already with a guy I met online and we came up with some interesting ideas. Basically one Revenants organization made up of Tzimisce Revenants with another organization with Cappadocians Revenants (including the Giovanni, Rossellini, and Dunsirn) plus some independent families.<br /> <br /> We thought about bumping up the power level a bit to make them a bit more fun too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't want to give too many details at the moment in what we already did (yet anyway) because I'd like some fresh ideas. Does anybody have some ideas along these lines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T23:20:17-07:00","id":1195148,"title":"","content":"Just to check - Vampire eliminated in the middle ages in an event that didn't (at the time) radically change how the Revenants operated then<br /> - Setting is Modern, so 800 or so years of no Vampiric influence<br /> <br /> First things first is within a few months (During the dark ages) all Revenants that lived beyond a normal Revenant's limit would die as the Vitae dried up.<br /> Ongoing, the Lines that have Fortitude in clan will prosper the most because their &quot;natural&quot; lifespan as a revenant is extended by about 50 years per dot of Fortitude.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that the Black Hand Revenants are still in existence, but changed, following the orders of the Mages into researching what happened to the vampires (and other supernatural?) While looking into other methods of immortality, Including Mummies and Risen. These Families probably can extend their life through True Magic, and possibly &quot;feed&quot; for extra blood points using Vitreous Path developed in the Underworld<br /> - Enrathi - Kidnapping test subjects and stealing information<br /> - Rafastio - Out in the real world as mystics and New agers, Crystal healing and the like.<br /> - Marijava - Thugs, Assassins and Spies. <br /> <br /> I think that Marijava would be dependant on Euthanatoi magic infusions since their old weakness isn't valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T07:01:26-07:00","id":1195715,"title":"","content":"Without Vampiric influence, I could easily imagine Revenents becoming public knowledge in the 20th century thanks to the rise of interest in eugenics. The Obertus would be into that kind of thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:11:41-07:00","id":1195884,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that they may be considered 'Vampires&quot; for their longevity and isolation, but with modern myths changed subtly, Garlic still repulsing them (Basarabs) etc.<br /> <br /> Your Bratovich will probably end up being the power player in modern nights.<br /> Not because they're smart or good leaders, but because of all of the Families; they are the best and maintaining breeding, so without Vampire oversight, families will live or die out at the displeasure of the Bratovich line.<br /> <br /> A handful of families that upset them may possibly interbreed and mix into one family, but they may have issues with Revenants not always breeding true, often getting children that don't have the blood and are just mortal. (Possible weaknesses of losing a clan discipline or slower blood generation than 1 per day)<br /> If they try to avoid this by inbreeding too much, you would have issues with mutations, physical or mental repercussions of a limited gene pool (limited attributes, derangements or mutations, ironically anaemia is common, which would affect blood pool, vitae generation or healing rate)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T23:14:20-07:00","id":1197053,"title":"","content":"Alright, let me tell y'all a few of the things I have so far.<br /> <br /> There are two different organizations of Revenants. There is the Genos which is made up of the families that once served the Tzimisce - The Zantosa, Grimaldi, Bratovich, Khazi, Obertus, Vlaszy, and maybe one other. There is also the Onorata Societ\u00e0 composed of the Giovanni, Rossellini, Dunsirn, and what we call the Minor Families (Rothstein, Pisanob, Ghiberti, etc.) Then there are a bunch of independent families, like the D'Habi or Marijava.<br /> <br /> Like the vampires would have, the families have their own political struggles and rivalries or alliances. The Zantosa were formerly the political movers and shakers of the Genos but they have declined in worldly power compared to the Grimaldi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}